# System Fixes & Optimization Walkthrough

## Summary of Accomplished Improvements

### 1. Telemetry Push Bridge & Live Active Bus Sync ✅ RESOLVED
- **Root Cause**: Engine's batch flush was firing up to 20 un-awaited concurrent HTTP POST requests every 500ms to `http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/admin/monitor/push`, overwhelming the Node.js Express server on Windows and dropping socket connections.
- **Fix**: Consolidated `startBatchFlush()` in [adminMonitor.ts (Engine)](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/engine/src/services/adminMonitor.ts) to push a single structured batch payload every 1000ms.
- **Outcome**: The Backend `/monitor/push` route now receives all active buses cleanly, updating `adminMonitor.activeBuses` and `mockDb.bus_live_state`.

### 2. Dual Data.json Persistence Across Server Reboots ✅ RESOLVED
- **Root Cause**: When Engine created dynamic routes or geocoded stops, `persistMockDb()` only wrote to `apps/engine/src/db/data.json`. The Backend maintained an isolated `apps/backend/src/db/data.json` that never received these updates. On server reboot, Backend reloaded its original 5,053 routes.
- **Fix**: Updated `persistMockDb()` in both [db/index.ts (Engine)](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/engine/src/db/index.ts) and [db/index.ts (Backend)](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/db/index.ts) to write changes to both file paths simultaneously.
- **Outcome**: Newly seeded routes and geocoded stops persist across server reboots in mock DB mode.

### 3. Continuous Background Historical Data Scraping ✅ RESOLVED
- **Root Cause**: Backend's `historicalDataScraper` relies on `adminMonitor.getActiveBuses()`. Since Backend previously had 0 active buses due to the push bridge issue, the scraper continuously logged `Scraper waiting for active buses from engine...`.
- **Fix**: Resolving the telemetry push bridge feeds the active bus list into Backend's `adminMonitor`, allowing `historicalDataScraper` to continuously run and log historical GPS records.

### 4. Continuous Real-Time Engine Log Stream in Admin UI ✅ RESOLVED
- **Root Cause**: `adapter_live.ts` only logged fetch events when `buses.length !== lastFetchCount`. Since Margdarshi API returns ~9,576 buses every cycle, no logs were generated after cycle 1.
- **Fix**: Removed the equality guard and added structured cycle summary and batch milestone logging to `adminMonitor` on every fetch cycle.
- **Outcome**: The Engine terminal tab on the Admin UI console streams live telemetry and processing events continuously.

### 5. Next.js 16 Turbopack Watcher Scoping & Config Fix ✅ RESOLVED
- **Root Cause**: Setting `turbopack.root` to `../../` caused Turbopack to watch the entire parent `upbus` directory. Every time Engine/Backend updated `data.json`, Turbopack detected a file change and entered an infinite recompilation/watcher lock on Windows, preventing page load.
- **Fix**: Updated [next.config.ts (Admin)](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/admin/next.config.ts) and [next.config.ts (Web App)](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/web-app/next.config.ts) to scope Turbopack's root strictly to `path.resolve(__dirname)`.
- **Outcome**: Admin UI loads pages instantly on `http://localhost:3003` without getting locked by parent directory file writes.

### 6. Fail-Safe Data.json Loading in Engine & Backend ✅ RESOLVED
- **Root Cause**: `require('./data.json')` in `apps/engine/src/db/index.ts` threw `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` when `data.json` was missing in `apps/engine/src/db/`.
- **Fix**: Replaced hardcoded `require('./data.json')` with fail-safe file resolution that checks local path first and falls back to `apps/backend/src/db/data.json`. Also copied `data.json` to `apps/engine/src/db/data.json`.
- **Outcome**: Engine starts smoothly without `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` errors.

